            <ArticleTitle>Simvastatin over the counter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In July 2004, simvastatin 10mg was reclassified in the UK from a Prescription-only medicine (PoM) to a Pharmacy (P) medicine and launched as Zocor Heart-Pro (Johnson &amp; Johnson. MSD Consumer Pharmaceuticals). It is the first statin in the world to be sold without prescription. Zocor Heart-Pro is licensed to reduce the risk of a first major coronary heart disease (CHD) event in people likely to be at &quot;moderate risk&quot; of such problems. Here we review the rationale and process for reclassifying simvastatin 10mg as an over-the-counter product.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
